WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.730
One laptop in a school
IT room picks up a virus.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.330
Then, one by one, PCs
across the school turn red.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.370
Rewind.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.710
On a normal day, those same links let a
file saved in one room open in another.

5
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.190
Every PC shares a few printers,
plus a single internet connection.

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.110
Overnight, every machine is
backed up from one place.

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.010
So if networks let a virus spread, why
does every school still connect its PCs?

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.750
In this mission, you'll
see what a network is,

9
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.190
and weigh its gains against
its costs: hardware,

10
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.710
skilled staff, and many users
hit if a central server fails.

11
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.320
Your mission: decide why schools
connect their PCs despite the risk.
